We introduce an online, incremental algorithm for efficiently executing Markov decision process (MDP) policies, featuring a time complexity of $T \log T + T^2/S$. This performance represents a substantial improvement over the leading method, SHIELD, reducing it from $T^2/S$. We also establish a lower bound of $\Omega(T \log T)$ for this problem, demonstrating that our proposed approach is theoretically near-optimal. MLE is not the only way to achieve this result; other online machine learning techniques can be used to reach similar outcomes.
